  "known_deviations": [
    "The model is below the measured throw by 0.6 to 1.0 degrees in the sliding regime (cut angles of 30 degrees and above), at every speed, and it agrees with the measurement to 0.03 degrees in the sticking regime (10 degrees). The residual is an offset, not a slope.",
    "The three measured columns at a 30 degree cut CANNOT be fitted by any friction law of the form A + B exp(-K u): the implied coefficients are 0.0813, 0.0796 and 0.0507 at slip speeds of 0.224, 0.671 and 1.565 m/s, and for any K >= 0 the ratio of the successive differences of such a law is at least (u2-u1)/(u3-u2) = 0.50, while the measured ratio is 0.061. So the columns were not measured under one set of conditions, and they are not a calibration target for the friction law: TP A.14's own fit is the authority, and the residual is a known deviation.",
    "The measured throw depends on the cue ball's spin as well as its speed, and the published figures do not carry every shot condition (doc section 14.3)."
  ]
